      "side": 1,
      "message": "I would guess that people requesting RTT ranging are going to request a lot of different ranges over time.  Given that, I would structure this interface more like:\n\n  // Obtain a reference to a IRttService that can be used to\n  // request ranging information.  Results will be returned\n  // via the registered IRttClient.\n  IRttService registerRttClient(IRttClient rttClient);\n  void unregisterRttClient(IRttClient rttClient);\n\nThen you can request RTT information, cancel requests, etc all through the IRttService.\n\nThis gives us a natural place to express having more than one client, each of which having its own set of pending requests.\n\n\nIs that over engineering?  I note that cancelRttRange() is a global operation and doesn\u0027t seem to support multiple clients very well.",
